ded above, while normal has support over all real values","Lognormal can also equal $0$, while normal has support over all real values","Lognormal takes all real values, like the normal it is built from"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"dddd19b3c19c92069c8bec88","time_limit":30},{"id":"pt_batch8_lognormal_distribution_001_curated20261027_001","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $Y\\sim\\mathcal{N}(\\mu,\\sigma^2)$ with $\\sigma>0$. Which random variable has a lognormal distribution with parameters $\\mu$ and $\\sigma^2$?","options":["$X=\\ln Y$","$X=|Y|$","$X=Y^2$","$X=\\mathrm{e}^{Y}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"09b27d54af00867ca8310696","time_limit":25},{"id":"pt_batch8_lognormal_distribution_014_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $\\ln X\\sim\\mathcal{N}(2,9)$. What is the median of $X$?","options":["$2$","$\\mathrm{e}^{2}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{6.5}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{-7}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"d71aa41daa70cc145bf42799","time_limit":30},{"id":"pt_batch8_lognormal_distribution_017_curated20261027_003","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $Y\\sim\\mathcal{N}(\\mu,\\sigma^2)$ with $\\sigma>0$ and $X=\\mathrm{e}^{Y}$. Why is $X$ right-skewed although $Y$ is symmetric about $\\mu$?","options":["A deviation $+t$ of $Y$ from $\\mu$ moves $X$ further than a deviation $-t$","$Y$ is itself right-skewed, and exponentiating keeps that skew","The mean $\\mu$ must be positive, which pushes the mass of $X$ right","A deviation $-t$ of $Y$ from $\\mu$ moves $X$ further than a deviation $+t$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"364743dbe2e7b7edf81d1219","time_limit":50},{"id":"pt_batch8_lognormal_distribution_019_curated20261027_004","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $\\ln X\\sim\\mathcal{N}(1,4)$ and let $\\Phi$ be the standard normal CDF. What is $\\mathbb{P}(X\\le\\mathrm{e}^{3})$?","options":["$\\Phi(0.5)$","$\\Phi(2)$","$\\Phi\\bigl((\\mathrm{e}^{3}-1)/2\\bigr)$","$\\Phi(1)$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a458ac5fadd4aba0204238c4","time_limit":30},{"id":"year_1_1b_probability_theory_for_eor_lognormal_distribution_3fc8bebe_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $X=\\mathrm{e}^{Y}$ with $Y\\sim\\mathcal{N}(-1,16)$, so that $X$ is lognormal with parameters $\\mu=-1$ and $\\sigma^2=16$. What is $\\mathbb{E}[X]$?","options":["$\\mathrm{e}^{-1}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{1}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{15}$","$\\mathrm{e}^{7}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"edb40af77e7cfb7c3fd4904f","time_limit":30}]}}